[Music]  on thursday in the midst of multiple  reports that washington quarterback alex  smith has an infection that was a result  of surgery to repair the leg that was  broken back in november washington  issued this statement on behalf of alex  smith we appreciate all the concerns and  prayers over the injury alex suffered on  november 18 against the texans although  this is a serious injury alex and his  family remain strong we would ask that  everyone please honor the smith family's  request for privacy at this time it  doesn't really confirm anything but at a  time when there are multiple reports  that there is an infection the result of  that surgery and these infections are  not uncommon i can recall rob gronkowski  the patriots tight end after he broke  his arm while  blocking  on an extra point play several years ago  he had a plate put in the arm they had  to replace the plate there was an  infection he had a picc line i mean it  was bad for him and he fought through  that over and over again after five  surgeries i think was the final total  tom brady had an infection after he had  acl repair surgery in 2008 infections do  happen we're so conditioned to think  that it's it's like taking your car in  for servicing when one of these  professional athletes especially  football players have some sort of  surgical procedure it is a serious  procedure anytime you have  your body cut open by a surgeon it is  not a good thing and there is a chance  that there could be complications so  with alex smith whatever the situation  is we wish him the best and we hope  number one he gets back to normal and  then number two that we see him back on  a football field but some of the reports  have characterized the condition as  potentially career ending and it really  wouldn't be a shock when you consider  the gravity of the injury joe theismann  never played again after suffering the  compound fracture in his lower leg in  1985 and there is a chance that alex  smith may not return and he's got a lot  of football left if he's able to play  he's still only 34 years old so we wish  him all the best number one for his  health for his long-term well-being but  also so he can continue his football  career if that's what he truly wants to  do as washington moves forward now  without alex smith without colt mccoy  and it's mark sanchez and josh johnson  the rest of the way  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

